# term-drag-k (M8): the equation's terms drag as their rulers do (D13, useTermDrags.ts). The pointer
# on k's term in the form line (202, 289, 33 x 24 in the reference's DOM: its centre (218, 301)): its
# tip "k = 0.00 · vertical shift", k's terms lit in both lines; a press drags at once (no threshold):
# k's ruler under its row, its band; 50 px right is 1.00 (0.02 a px), the live line holding the
# term; the release lets go; a double-click resets k to 0 as its second click lets go: a frame into
# the spring to the reset value (FV 05's jump; M10 made the port's), and at rest.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 2000
move 218 301
wait 500
shot hover
down
wait 16
move 268 301 over 160
wait 16
shot held
up
wait 16
shot released
# Past the double-click time since the drag's press (500 ms, SDL's and a browser's), so the double
# click's first press counts as a first click on every surface: Playwright's synthetic clicks count
# from 1, SDL counts on from the drag's press.
wait 600
dblclick 218 301
wait 16
shot reset
wait 1484
shot reset-rest
